"\n30: mkdir -p recalc pdf\n31: soffice --headless \"-env:UserInstallation=file://$profile\" \\\n32:   --convert-to xlsx --outdir recalc output.xlsx\n33: soffice --headless \"-env:UserInstallation=file://$profile\" \\\n34:   --convert-to pdf --outdir pdf recalc/output.xlsx\n35: pdftoppm -png -r 144 pdf/output.pdf pdf/page\n36: ```\n37: \n38: Use the recalculated workbook as the final artifact only after checking that it\n39: did not lose required features. Inspect formula cells for errors such as\n40: `#REF!`, `#DIV/0!`, `#VALUE!`, and `#NAME?`, and visually inspect rendered\n41: pages for truncated columns, bad number formats, and broken charts.\n42: \n43: ## Authoring rules\n44: \n45: - Keep calculations auditable: place formulas in cells instead of only in\n46:   scripts whenever the workbook is meant to be edited by users.\n47: - Apply appropriate number/date formats, column widths, freeze panes, and\n48:   filters when they improve usability.\n49: - Never overwrite the source workbook unless the task explicitly asks for it.\n\n(End of file - total 49 lines)\n</content>","type":"function_call_output","id":null,"status":null},{"arguments":"{\"command\": \"python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport openpyxl, glob\\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob('/workspace/input/*.xlsx')):\\n    wb = openpyxl.load_workbook(f, data_only=True)\\n    print('='*80)\\n    print(f)\\n    for ws in wb.worksheets:\\n        print(f'  Sheet: {ws.title}  dims={ws.dimensions}  max_row={ws.max_row} max_col={ws.max_column}')\\nEOF\", \"description\": \"Inspect sheet names and dimensions of input workbooks\"}","call_id":"bash_0_57cfbdd4","name":"bash","type":"function_call","id":null,"status":null,"namespace":null},{"call_id":"bash_0_57cfbdd4","output":"================================================================================\n/workspace/input/4-financial-table-income-expense-dashboard.xlsx\n  Sheet: Income Expense Dashboard  dims=A1:XDD38  max_row=38 max_col=16332\n  Sheet: Income Details  dims=A2:J47  max_row=47 max_col=10\n  Sheet: Expense Details  dims=A1:XFD47  max_row=47 max_col=16384\n================================================================================\n/workspace/input/5-financial-table-income-expense-profit-statement_visual-charts_.xlsx\n  Sheet: Sheet1  dims=A1:AD24  max_row=24 max_col=30\n  Sheet: Income Expense Details  dims=B2:M36  max_row=36 max_col=13\n================================================================================\n/workspace/input/6-financial-table-income-and-expense-data-visual-charts.xlsx\n  Sheet: Sheet1  dims=B2:X18  max_row=18 max_col=24\n","type":"function_call_output","id":null,"status":null},{"arguments":"{\"command\": \"python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport openpyxl\\ndef dump(f, sheet, max_r=50, max_c=15):\\n    wb = openpyxl.load_workbook(f, data_only=True)\\n    ws = wb[sheet]\\n    print('#'*90)\\n    print(f, '->', sheet)\\n    for r in ws.iter_rows(min_row=1, max_row=min(ws.max_row,max_r), max_col=min(ws.max_column,max_c)):\\n        vals = [(c.coordinate, c.value) for c in r if c.value is not None]\\n        if vals: print(vals)\\n\\ndump('/workspace/input/4-financial-table-income-expense-dashboard.xlsx','Income Expense Dashboard', max_r=38, max_c=10)\\ndump('/workspace/input/4-financial-table-income-expense-dashboard.xlsx','Expense Details', max_r=47, max_c=10)\\nEOF\", \"description\": \"Dump dashboard and expense details sheets\"}","call_id":"bash_0_50ddee34","name":"bash","type":"function_call","id":null,"status":null,"namespace":null},{"call_id":"bash_0_50ddee34","output":"##########################################################################################\n/workspace/input/4-financial-table-income-expense-dashboard.xlsx -> Income Expense Dashboard\n[('B2', 'Financial Management - Income Expense Dashboard')]\n[('B5', 2021), ('D5', 'Year'), ('E5', 5), ('F5', 'Month'), ('J5', 'Daily Summary')]\n[('B6', 'Sun'), ('C6', 'Mon'), ('D6', 'Tue'), ('E6', 'Wed'), ('F6', 'Thu'), ('G6', 'Fri'), ('H6', 'Sat'), ('J6', 'Da